Exp32 frozen — Track B RANGE COMPRESSION -> NEXT-DAY RANGE EXPANSION. Use completed M5 broker-days strictly before 2026-08-13 00:00 BRT and unconditionally drop first/last file-edge broker-days. Define DayRange_d=High_d-Low_d. Define RangeRef20_d as the median DayRange of the previous 20 completed broker-days only, excluding day d. Define RangeRatio_d=DayRange_d/RangeRef20_d. Target y_expand_d=1 iff RangeRatio_d>1. Feature PrevCompress_d=1 iff RangeRatio_{d-1}<1, where the prior-day ratio itself uses only data available through d-1. Eligible target days require a valid current RangeRef20 and valid prior-day RangeRatio. Build ISO broker-week keys after feature construction and assign whole eligible ISO weeks chronologically 60/20/20 to TRAIN/VALIDATION/TEST; no week may straddle splits.

Exp32 BASE is TRAIN constant P(y_expand=1). EXTENDED freezes BASE and fits exactly one TRAIN coefficient k_compress applied only when PrevCompress=1; PrevCompress=0 predictions remain identical. Primary unit=completed broker-day, primary estimand=DAY_WEIGHTED, dependence-aware uncertainty=resamples whole ISO broker-weeks and computes total gain / total sampled target days. Survival requires Brier and LogLoss gain CI95>0 in BOTH Validation and TEST. Previous-compression/previous-expansion observed rates are diagnostics only. No alternate lookback 10/30/60, quantile thresholds, consecutive-compression streaks, direction conditioning, ATR/body/wick/volume replacement, weekday/D1/Clock/Z/Fib/Track-D interaction, polynomial/spline or threshold rescue. If Exp32 fails, reject this exact one-day compression indicator with 20-day rolling-median range reference and move to a different predeclared Track-B family. Historical OOS remains exploratory. Exp27 remains untouched. Runtime promotion NONE.